1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,411
Merchant of Joseon

2
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:50,689
Episode 1

3
00:01:18,879 --> 00:01:22,181
There are a lot of good interpreters.

4
00:01:22,182 --> 00:01:23,627
To be the best interpreter,

5
00:01:23,684 --> 00:01:26,324
you have to be educated.

6
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:29,965
And you can't even remember
simple dialects.

7
00:01:30,924 --> 00:01:32,925
I'm sorry.
Please forgive me.

8
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:35,497
I'll strike you 10 times.
Keep count.

9
00:01:36,763 --> 00:01:38,297
Father, please forgive me.

10
00:01:38,298 --> 00:01:39,470
You!

11
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,404
I told you not to speak Korean
when studying.

12
00:01:44,071 --> 00:01:45,471
1...

13
00:01:45,472 --> 00:01:48,975
2... 3...

14
00:01:48,976 --> 00:01:53,976
4... 5... 6...
7... 8... 9...

15
00:02:00,988 --> 00:02:03,525
Hey, wait a minute.

16
00:02:03,590 --> 00:02:05,399
I'm busy.

17
00:02:05,459 --> 00:02:07,063
Just wait.

18
00:02:07,694 --> 00:02:13,007
I'm late and the boat is packed.
You have to take the next boat.

19
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:16,570
I can't. You have to take me.

20
00:02:16,803 --> 00:02:20,606
I have to be
at Boreum village by noon.

21
00:02:20,607 --> 00:02:22,143
I have to take this boat.

22
00:02:23,911 --> 00:02:26,653
I told you there's no space.

23
00:02:26,713 --> 00:02:29,319
Take the next one in an hour.

24
00:02:29,383 --> 00:02:32,660
Please, I have to take the boat.

25
00:02:32,719 --> 00:02:36,030
Otherwise my salt sales
will be ruined.

26
00:02:36,089 --> 00:02:38,090
I said, no.

27
00:02:38,091 --> 00:02:39,759
Just wait a minute.

28
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,994
Hey, are we leaving or not?

29
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:45,431
We're busy here.
Get going.

30
00:02:45,432 --> 00:02:46,342
Yes, sir.

31
00:02:46,466 --> 00:02:49,709
I said there's no room.

32
00:02:50,904 --> 00:02:51,771
Mr. Boatman.

33
00:02:51,772 --> 00:02:52,772
Here's your salt.

34
00:02:52,773 --> 00:02:54,480
My Salt!

35
00:02:55,442 --> 00:02:59,584
You have to take me.

36
00:02:59,646 --> 00:03:04,493
The next boat will be too late.
Mr. Boatman!

37
00:03:08,622 --> 00:03:12,661
Look at all my salt...

38
00:03:18,465 --> 00:03:21,309
Mother, what happened to the salt?

39
00:03:21,501 --> 00:03:23,310
What happened?

40
00:03:30,677 --> 00:03:32,088
Mother, are you ill?

41
00:03:32,779 --> 00:03:37,125
No, I spilled the salt.

42
00:03:37,551 --> 00:03:39,087
I must've tripped on something.

43
00:03:40,721 --> 00:03:42,655
Did you miss the boat?

44
00:03:42,656 --> 00:03:47,105
No, I'm going to take the next one.

45
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:50,801
I'm so forgetful these days.

46
00:03:51,198 --> 00:03:54,500
A woman can't sell salt.

47
00:03:54,501 --> 00:03:57,414
That's a man's job.

48
00:03:57,471 --> 00:04:01,442
That wouldn't happen to a man.

49
00:04:01,508 --> 00:04:05,081
Yeah, too bad.
Let's get going.

50
00:04:05,145 --> 00:04:06,283
Yeah.

51
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:50,292
Please buy my merchandise.
Please...

52
00:04:54,795 --> 00:04:58,299
Look at the fur. It's the best.

53
00:04:59,066 --> 00:05:01,512
Look at the fur. It's the best.

54
00:05:02,803 --> 00:05:04,476
I'm telling you. It's the best.

55
00:05:06,173 --> 00:05:10,810
Sang-ok, come here quick.

56
00:05:10,811 --> 00:05:15,055
Tell him 8 otter furs
for a roll of silk.

57
00:05:15,115 --> 00:05:17,149
This fur is even offered to the King.

58
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:19,819
Look at this fur. It's perfect.

59
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:22,955
He won't find anything better.

60
00:05:22,956 --> 00:05:24,765
Translate, quickly.

61
00:05:25,258 --> 00:05:28,828
He'll give you 8 otter furs
for a roll of silk.

62
00:05:28,829 --> 00:05:30,162
8 otter furs?

63
00:05:30,163 --> 00:05:32,965
This fur is even offered to the King.

64
00:05:32,966 --> 00:05:37,176
You won't find anything better.

65
00:05:37,971 --> 00:05:41,507
You're very bright. I'll take it.

66
00:05:41,508 --> 00:05:44,210
He'll take the deal.

67
00:05:44,211 --> 00:05:45,383
Really?

68
00:05:48,448 --> 00:05:50,382
Here, good job.

69
00:05:50,383 --> 00:05:51,657
Thank you.

70
00:05:55,589 --> 00:05:56,789
Sang-ok, come here.

71
00:05:56,790 --> 00:05:57,490
Yes.

72
00:05:57,491 --> 00:05:59,437
I need your help.

73
00:05:59,493 --> 00:06:03,566
Tell him 10jade hair pins
and 5 rings for 5 nyang.

74
00:06:04,331 --> 00:06:09,474
10 jade hair pins
and 5 rings for 5 nyang.

75
00:06:11,605 --> 00:06:15,975
You're such a good help.
Good job.

76
00:06:15,976 --> 00:06:17,717
Thank you.

77
00:06:22,249 --> 00:06:23,421
2 nyan9-

78
00:06:23,517 --> 00:06:24,587
2 nyan9-

79
00:06:27,988 --> 00:06:28,854
Good job.

80
00:06:28,855 --> 00:06:30,198
Thank you.

81
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:34,532
Mother.

82
00:06:39,566 --> 00:06:40,738
Jeez...

83
00:06:42,903 --> 00:06:44,109
Mother.

84
00:07:00,754 --> 00:07:02,825
Don't come to the ferry again.

85
00:07:04,057 --> 00:07:09,057
Father said that I have to speak
with Chinese people to practice.

86
00:07:09,796 --> 00:07:14,245
He told you to learn the language,
not earn petty money off of it.

87
00:07:15,835 --> 00:07:21,183
A man has to be determined,
even if you're poor.

88
00:07:22,075 --> 00:07:24,885
A man's destiny is
what you make of it.

89
00:07:25,779 --> 00:07:30,250
You just study and
become an interpreter.

90
00:07:30,617 --> 00:07:34,720
Dad studied all his life,
but didn't make it.

91
00:07:34,721 --> 00:07:36,064
Your father...

92
00:07:38,525 --> 00:07:40,664
He didn't have the luck.

93
00:07:42,162 --> 00:07:45,700
He's good,
he just had bad luck.

94
00:07:46,766 --> 00:07:50,908
He didn't make it
because of the corruption.

95
00:07:52,239 --> 00:07:57,450
If he meets an honest exam supervisor,
he'll become the best interpreter.

96
00:07:58,445 --> 00:08:01,255
I hate that you're working so hard.

97
00:08:01,381 --> 00:08:04,919
I hate being so poor.

98
00:08:04,985 --> 00:08:08,023
A lot of people are worse off
than we are.

99
00:08:09,856 --> 00:08:15,829
My back kills me
when I walk so much.

100
00:08:17,264 --> 00:08:20,973
It tires me out.

101
00:08:22,469 --> 00:08:27,111
But I never blamed
your father for this.

102
00:08:28,108 --> 00:08:32,181
And he never gave up.

103
00:08:33,446 --> 00:08:35,187
When a man makes up his mind,

104
00:08:35,782 --> 00:08:41,460
you never give up no matter what.

105
00:08:49,162 --> 00:08:52,575
It's smooth and perfect.

106
00:08:54,301 --> 00:08:56,110
This one's good, too.

107
00:08:56,336 --> 00:08:58,839
Look at how smooth it is.

108
00:09:00,140 --> 00:09:01,551
Sang-ok.

109
00:09:02,008 --> 00:09:04,576
Come interpret for me.

110
00:09:04,577 --> 00:09:06,420
I'll pay you.

111
00:09:06,579 --> 00:09:08,581
I don't do that anymore.

112
00:09:08,648 --> 00:09:13,188
What do you mean?
Sang-ok, come on.

113
00:09:20,894 --> 00:09:22,430
Bok-tae, Eok-swe!

114
00:09:22,696 --> 00:09:26,234
Where do you think
you're going?

115
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:28,934
Get Up!

116
00:09:28,935 --> 00:09:32,382
We're sorry.
Please forgive us.

117
00:09:32,439 --> 00:09:34,942
How could you lose that money?

118
00:09:35,008 --> 00:09:37,376
We're sorry. Please forgive us.

119
00:09:37,377 --> 00:09:39,755
You don't deserve to live.

120
00:09:40,447 --> 00:09:43,182
We're sorry.

121
00:09:43,183 --> 00:09:45,322
That money was important.

122
00:09:45,385 --> 00:09:49,021
Get out of my face.
Go get the money. Go get it.

123
00:09:49,022 --> 00:09:50,689
Stop, you'll kill them.

124
00:09:50,690 --> 00:09:53,959
Let me go.
They deserve to die.

125
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,394
If I buy barley with that money,

126
00:09:55,395 --> 00:09:57,996
we can eat it for the whole year.

127
00:09:57,997 --> 00:10:00,966
I worked so hard for it,

128
00:10:00,967 --> 00:10:02,801
and you go lose it?

129
00:10:02,802 --> 00:10:04,603
Come here.

130
00:10:04,604 --> 00:10:06,277
Stop it.

131
00:10:08,541 --> 00:10:10,976
You go find that money

132
00:10:10,977 --> 00:10:14,220
or don't ever come back,
you hear?

133
00:10:14,347 --> 00:10:15,451
Let's go.

134
00:10:26,793 --> 00:10:28,431
How did you lose the money?

135
00:10:28,762 --> 00:10:32,505
We lost his bundle.

136
00:10:32,832 --> 00:10:34,539
How much did you lose?

137
00:10:34,834 --> 00:10:35,744
Five jeon.

138
00:10:36,269 --> 00:10:37,339
What?

139
00:10:38,271 --> 00:10:39,138
Brother.

140
00:10:39,139 --> 00:10:40,372
Don't cry.

141
00:10:40,373 --> 00:10:44,048
He'll kill us if we don't find it.

142
00:10:44,110 --> 00:10:46,845
Stop crying, you idiot.

143
00:10:46,846 --> 00:10:50,115
We'll go somewhere else.
We can make money somewhere else.

144
00:10:50,116 --> 00:10:51,186
Stop it.

145
00:10:52,585 --> 00:10:53,859
I said, stop it.

146
00:10:54,287 --> 00:10:56,494
I'll get you the money.

147
00:11:22,615 --> 00:11:24,783
You two stay here.

148
00:11:24,784 --> 00:11:25,694
OK.

149
00:11:30,857 --> 00:11:31,801
What do you want?

150
00:11:32,292 --> 00:11:34,660
I'm here to see the owner.

151
00:11:34,661 --> 00:11:36,299
Why?

152
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:38,600
I need to talk to him.

153
00:11:38,665 --> 00:11:40,440
Are you kidding me?

154
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:42,446
What do you want to talk him about?

155
00:11:42,569 --> 00:11:44,310
It's very important.

156
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:47,749
Stop ruining the business
and go away.

157
00:11:47,841 --> 00:11:48,751
What's going on?

158
00:11:48,808 --> 00:11:50,116
Sir, he asked to see you.

159
00:11:50,176 --> 00:11:54,090
He says it's important.

160
00:11:55,348 --> 00:11:57,453
I don't know you.

161
00:11:57,517 --> 00:11:59,997
I'm Lim Sang-ok
from Jincheon Village.

162
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:01,824
What do you want?

163
00:12:02,822 --> 00:12:07,828
If you pay me 5 jeon,
I'll double your sales.

164
00:12:08,061 --> 00:12:10,632
Double my sales? How?

165
00:12:11,297 --> 00:12:15,905
I'll tell you after
you promise to pay me.

166
00:12:16,469 --> 00:12:20,417
I'll pay you 1 nyang if you do.

167
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:24,142
There's a village of a folk music group.
It's called Jein Village.

168
00:12:24,143 --> 00:12:27,056
The children are good musicians.

169
00:12:27,914 --> 00:12:31,020
I heard about them. So?

170
00:12:31,217 --> 00:12:35,787
I'll bring them here
and make them perform.

171
00:12:35,788 --> 00:12:37,589
People will come to see
the performance

172
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:40,002
and you can double your sales.

173
00:12:41,027 --> 00:12:43,729
They'll be busy watching the show.

174
00:12:43,730 --> 00:12:45,531
They won't buy anything.

175
00:12:45,532 --> 00:12:47,165
The sales will increase.

176
00:12:47,166 --> 00:12:50,079
Stop talking nonsense
and go home.

177
00:12:50,136 --> 00:12:51,809
Give him some money.

178
00:12:51,871 --> 00:12:52,975
Yes, sir.

179
00:12:53,072 --> 00:12:54,050
Let's go.

180
00:12:56,075 --> 00:12:59,177
Here, go buy yourself a snack.

181
00:12:59,178 --> 00:13:01,249
I'm not a beggar.

182
00:13:01,714 --> 00:13:04,160
That rude...

183
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:06,896
How did it go?

184
00:13:09,289 --> 00:13:11,326
Not as I planned.
But don't worry.

185
00:13:11,424 --> 00:13:13,870
Let's go.

186
00:13:15,428 --> 00:13:16,406
Hey.

187
00:13:20,033 --> 00:13:21,637
I'll pay you.

188
00:13:51,364 --> 00:13:53,207
There's Mogabi. Hide.

189
00:14:15,021 --> 00:14:17,695
Cho-rye... Cho-rye!

190
00:14:24,297 --> 00:14:25,367
Did you get the money?

191
00:14:27,066 --> 00:14:31,879
Mr. Mogabi will kill you.
Don't come here.

192
00:14:32,138 --> 00:14:33,242
Cho-rye.

193
00:14:39,946 --> 00:14:40,981
Really?

194
00:14:46,953 --> 00:14:47,988
L-lurFy-

195
00:15:19,385 --> 00:15:23,155
Where is everyone?

196
00:15:23,156 --> 00:15:29,232
Cho-rye. Darling?
Where are they? Cho-rye!

197
00:15:58,591 --> 00:16:03,591
Alright. Here.
Wait a minute. Here.

198
00:16:36,596 --> 00:16:41,596
This is 6 jeon,
more than you asked for.

199
00:16:41,701 --> 00:16:42,907
Thank you.

200
00:16:43,269 --> 00:16:46,171
You're very clever.

201
00:16:46,172 --> 00:16:49,174
You'll be a good businessman.

202
00:16:49,175 --> 00:16:52,622
I'll be the best interpreter
in Joseon.

203
00:16:52,712 --> 00:16:53,747
Huh?

204
00:17:04,757 --> 00:17:06,458
Hello.

205
00:17:06,459 --> 00:17:08,026
Do you speak Chinese?

206
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,861
Yes, my name is Lim Sang-ok.

207
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:11,730
I'd like to test my Chinese.

208
00:17:11,731 --> 00:17:13,231
If it's not too much trouble,

209
00:17:13,232 --> 00:17:15,200
I'd like to ask a few questions.

210
00:17:15,201 --> 00:17:17,536
OK, what do you want to know?

211
00:17:17,537 --> 00:17:19,771
How many times have
you been to Joseon?

212
00:17:19,772 --> 00:17:24,772
This is my third... No, forth visit.

213
00:17:25,111 --> 00:17:27,379
Where are you from?

214
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:30,282
Yanjing.

215
00:17:30,283 --> 00:17:32,617
How is Yanjing these days?

216
00:17:32,618 --> 00:17:35,554
I heard that the Emperor is ill.
Is it true?

217
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:38,456
You're practically a Chinese person.

218
00:17:38,457 --> 00:17:41,529
You're more up to date than I am.

219
00:17:41,594 --> 00:17:46,594
I could pass for a Chinese person?

220
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:48,800
Of course.

221
00:17:48,801 --> 00:17:53,171
You could pass for
a government official.

222
00:17:53,172 --> 00:17:54,150
Thank you.

223
00:18:04,116 --> 00:18:07,319
It's made with the best jade.

224
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:11,234
I'll give it to you for 5 nyang.

225
00:18:24,403 --> 00:18:33,790
How dare you steal from me?

226
00:18:38,284 --> 00:18:41,663
I'm sorry, please forgive me.

227
00:18:45,491 --> 00:18:46,324
What's this?

228
00:18:46,325 --> 00:18:50,328
He's just a kid.
You're being too cruel.

229
00:18:50,329 --> 00:18:53,198
This kid is a thief.

230
00:18:53,199 --> 00:18:55,901
I can't let a thief go unpunished.

231
00:18:55,902 --> 00:18:59,471
Then punish him
according to Joseon laws.

232
00:18:59,472 --> 00:19:00,939
Go away.

233
00:19:00,940 --> 00:19:03,141
This is none of your business.

234
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:05,520
Go or I'll teach you a lesson.

235
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:48,961
Don't ever come back here

236
00:19:49,355 --> 00:19:52,893
or I'll have you arrested.

237
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:58,897
Get goi"9-

238
00:19:58,898 --> 00:20:00,468
Thank you.

239
00:20:10,609 --> 00:20:11,485
Louder!

240
00:20:12,311 --> 00:20:13,312
Louder!

241
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:15,914
Right-hand strike!

242
00:20:15,915 --> 00:20:17,258
Smile!

243
00:20:17,750 --> 00:20:18,626
Turn!

244
00:20:19,652 --> 00:20:20,722
Turn!

245
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:22,563
Louder!

246
00:20:22,989 --> 00:20:24,434
Two hands!

247
00:20:24,657 --> 00:20:27,001
Spread your arms and jump.
A little more.

248
00:20:38,637 --> 00:20:42,244
Give me my money.
Give me my money.

249
00:20:42,308 --> 00:20:43,775
What did you say?

250
00:20:43,776 --> 00:20:47,112
I didn't do anything.
Bok-tae took him gambling.

251
00:20:47,113 --> 00:20:50,720
All I did was eat the free food.

252
00:20:50,950 --> 00:20:54,864
I'll kill you both.

253
00:20:54,954 --> 00:20:56,126
Sir...

254
00:20:57,156 --> 00:21:01,832
Hey, you stop right there.

255
00:21:02,228 --> 00:21:03,298
What do we do?

256
00:21:15,441 --> 00:21:16,647
Over there.

257
00:21:24,917 --> 00:21:26,117
There he is.

258
00:21:26,118 --> 00:21:27,062
Sang-ok.

259
00:21:28,587 --> 00:21:31,523
If we don't take care of
this by sun down,

260
00:21:31,524 --> 00:21:33,792
we're both dead.

261
00:21:33,793 --> 00:21:34,726
Please help us.

262
00:21:34,727 --> 00:21:36,928
I don't have time for games.

263
00:21:36,929 --> 00:21:37,996
Please.

264
00:21:37,997 --> 00:21:39,931
You know how Mogabi is.

265
00:21:39,932 --> 00:21:42,845
He's threatening to kill us.

266
00:21:43,035 --> 00:21:45,703
You gambled away the money.
You deserve it.

267
00:21:45,704 --> 00:21:47,911
Just help me.

268
00:21:48,007 --> 00:21:51,545
I can't come up with
that kind of money.

269
00:21:52,545 --> 00:21:55,924
I have an idea.
I just need your help.

270
00:21:57,316 --> 00:21:58,226
What's this?

271
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:00,088
Japanese silver coins.

272
00:22:00,619 --> 00:22:01,495
Japanese coins?

273
00:22:01,754 --> 00:22:02,960
What are you going
to do with them?

274
00:22:04,156 --> 00:22:06,727
We'll trade it
for Chinese silver coins.

275
00:22:06,792 --> 00:22:08,460
Trade two Japanese silvers
for one Chinese.

276
00:22:08,461 --> 00:22:09,961
It's worth 1 and a half.

277
00:22:09,962 --> 00:22:12,465
They'll be happy to do it.

278
00:22:13,265 --> 00:22:14,141
Are these yours?

279
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:17,613
I wouldn't trade it
if they were mine.

280
00:22:18,003 --> 00:22:20,040
It belongs to Yong-tae.

281
00:22:20,239 --> 00:22:23,152
He'll give me 5 nyang
if I trade them.

282
00:22:23,576 --> 00:22:28,457
Just interpret for us
when Eok-swe brings a Chinese.

283
00:22:29,815 --> 00:22:31,192
Here they come.

284
00:22:31,851 --> 00:22:33,091
Talk.

285
00:22:35,421 --> 00:22:36,627
And say what?

286
00:22:36,922 --> 00:22:39,198
Didn't you hear anything?

287
00:22:43,162 --> 00:22:47,599
We'll trade 2 Japanese coins
for 1 Chinese.

288
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:51,980
It's worth 1 and a half. We're trading
cheap because we're in a rush.

289
00:22:53,439 --> 00:22:54,539
Is this genuine?

290
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:55,406
What did he say?

291
00:22:55,407 --> 00:22:56,708
He's asking if it's genuine.

292
00:22:56,709 --> 00:22:58,810
Of course it is.

293
00:22:58,811 --> 00:22:59,915
It's genuine.

294
00:23:00,779 --> 00:23:02,452
Genuine.

295
00:23:02,548 --> 00:23:04,186
What do you think you're doing?

296
00:23:04,617 --> 00:23:06,654
Who are you?

297
00:23:06,886 --> 00:23:09,120
Deceiving Chinese merchants
with counterfeits

298
00:23:09,121 --> 00:23:12,432
can discredit
all Joseon merchants.

299
00:23:13,325 --> 00:23:14,592
What's going on?

300
00:23:14,593 --> 00:23:15,731
This isn't counterfeit.

301
00:23:15,961 --> 00:23:18,532
Mind your own business.

302
00:23:19,165 --> 00:23:22,300
Japanese silver hasn't
been used for decades.

303
00:23:22,301 --> 00:23:23,541
This is a counterfeit.

304
00:23:24,336 --> 00:23:26,337
Hey, that's enough.

305
00:23:26,338 --> 00:23:27,976
Go away.

306
00:23:28,574 --> 00:23:33,284
You're ruining the commerce.
Go away.

307
00:23:36,182 --> 00:23:37,855
Damn it.

308
00:23:37,983 --> 00:23:42,693
What a crappy day.

309
00:23:42,788 --> 00:23:45,496
What do they know?

310
00:23:45,591 --> 00:23:47,358
Hey, don't worry.

311
00:23:47,359 --> 00:23:50,203
Are you sure that this is genuine?

312
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:53,402
Do you trust me
or some stranger?

313
00:23:53,465 --> 00:23:56,501


314
00:23:56,502 --> 00:23:57,845
Hey, where are you going?

315
00:23:59,338 --> 00:24:02,114
Say something.

316
00:24:02,608 --> 00:24:04,781
OK.
{Stop right there.

317
00:24:08,214 --> 00:24:10,455
Hey. What's going on?

318
00:24:10,516 --> 00:24:12,826
What did I do?

319
00:24:14,420 --> 00:24:16,422
I don't know anything.

320
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:03,707
I'm sorry.
Forgive me just once.

321
00:25:03,769 --> 00:25:06,537
I'm ashamed that I even know you.

322
00:25:06,538 --> 00:25:07,972
Don't ever talk to me again.

323
00:25:07,973 --> 00:25:09,611
We're sorry.

324
00:25:09,675 --> 00:25:13,177
I don't want anything
to do with you two.

325
00:25:13,178 --> 00:25:16,481
We were that desperate.

326
00:25:16,482 --> 00:25:19,117
We won't do it again.
Come on.

327
00:25:19,118 --> 00:25:20,028
Let me go.

328
00:25:20,085 --> 00:25:21,996
Sang-ok.
{Forgive us.

329
00:25:22,054 --> 00:25:23,590
Let me go
{I'm sorry.

330
00:25:23,656 --> 00:25:26,724
Let me go.
II said I'm sorry.

331
00:25:26,725 --> 00:25:29,569
Hey, look.

332
00:25:31,930 --> 00:25:33,876
They reported us.

333
00:25:33,932 --> 00:25:35,070
Hey, you.

334
00:25:40,439 --> 00:25:43,545
Hey, who the hell are you?

335
00:25:43,709 --> 00:25:45,814
You reported us

336
00:25:45,878 --> 00:25:47,679
and we got a beating.

337
00:25:47,680 --> 00:25:49,091
Stop it.

338
00:25:49,214 --> 00:25:51,820
You were the one
deceiving the Chinese.

339
00:25:51,950 --> 00:25:54,863
I just want to talk.

340
00:25:54,987 --> 00:25:56,193
Stop it.

341
00:25:57,556 --> 00:25:59,331
I apologize for their rude behavior.

342
00:26:07,566 --> 00:26:08,806
What are you doing?

343
00:26:08,901 --> 00:26:11,108
What did he do?

344
00:26:11,236 --> 00:26:13,978
Who are you?
What did we do?

345
00:26:14,873 --> 00:26:16,284
What did we do?

346
00:26:16,508 --> 00:26:18,647
Why...

347
00:26:21,213 --> 00:26:21,987
Hit 'em.

348
00:26:54,646 --> 00:26:56,848
What's going on?
Stop this instant!

349
00:26:56,849 --> 00:26:58,683
What did we do to deserve this?

350
00:26:58,684 --> 00:27:02,393
Don't you people know
any business manners?

351
00:27:02,454 --> 00:27:06,925
You think you can take our business
from right under our nose?

352
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:10,338
All you do is ruin the market.

353
00:27:10,396 --> 00:27:12,263
We don't want you here.

354
00:27:12,264 --> 00:27:14,471
This is a misunderstanding.

355
00:27:14,533 --> 00:27:16,567
We didn't do anything wrong.

356
00:27:16,568 --> 00:27:17,945
Shut up.

357
00:27:18,203 --> 00:27:21,514
You people are taking
all the business.

358
00:27:21,573 --> 00:27:24,110
Everyone knows that.

359
00:27:24,510 --> 00:27:28,813
You come here
to take our business,

360
00:27:28,814 --> 00:27:30,885
and you think we'll just watch?

361
00:27:30,983 --> 00:27:34,396
What are you talking about?
We have the government's approval.

362
00:27:34,453 --> 00:27:38,367
Shut up,
you don't belong here.

363
00:27:38,424 --> 00:27:40,062
This isn't your town.

364
00:27:40,125 --> 00:27:43,265
What are you waiting for?
Get rid of them.

365
00:27:57,109 --> 00:28:00,682
It was going to happen
once anyway.

366
00:28:01,780 --> 00:28:03,885
They're reacting like this

367
00:28:04,183 --> 00:28:07,323
because we're threatening them.

368
00:28:07,719 --> 00:28:10,199
It was a chance to let others

369
00:28:10,255 --> 00:28:12,929
know about our existence.

370
00:28:13,325 --> 00:28:15,498
It was a benefit to us at the end.

371
00:28:17,062 --> 00:28:21,101
How badly hurt are the merchants?

372
00:28:21,967 --> 00:28:25,141
Don't worry.
The doctor came by.

373
00:28:49,895 --> 00:28:52,808
We make a living with our face.

374
00:28:52,898 --> 00:28:55,674
We're clowns that perform
in front of people.

375
00:28:55,734 --> 00:29:00,404
Look at them.
They're bleeding cripples.

376
00:29:00,405 --> 00:29:04,080
How can you look the other way?

377
00:29:04,810 --> 00:29:06,847
It's got nothing to do with us.

378
00:29:06,912 --> 00:29:09,180
Go to rival merchants
for compensation.

379
00:29:09,181 --> 00:29:11,320
I can't believe this.

380
00:29:11,450 --> 00:29:14,192
They thought
our boys worked for you.

381
00:29:14,253 --> 00:29:16,733
And it's got nothing to do with you?
How can you ignore that?

382
00:29:16,788 --> 00:29:19,234
And Sang-ok almost died.

383
00:29:19,291 --> 00:29:22,431
He's not even
a performer like us.

384
00:29:22,494 --> 00:29:26,203
He's studying so hard
to be an interpreter.

385
00:29:26,265 --> 00:29:29,610
Poor Sang-ok.

386
00:29:29,701 --> 00:29:33,171
Sang-ok...

387
00:29:33,238 --> 00:29:34,376
Sang-ok.

388
00:29:42,247 --> 00:29:44,591
Stop making trouble and go away.

389
00:29:45,017 --> 00:29:47,752
Sir, think of it as charity

390
00:29:47,753 --> 00:29:53,863
and give a little money
for some medicine.

391
00:30:00,632 --> 00:30:05,411
Sir. Sir!

392
00:30:07,439 --> 00:30:08,543


393
00:30:09,241 --> 00:30:10,447
Jerks.

394
00:30:11,243 --> 00:30:13,587
You two are so dead.

395
00:30:18,750 --> 00:30:20,127


396
00:30:20,252 --> 00:30:22,386
Sang-ok, that woman...

397
00:30:22,387 --> 00:30:25,630
She's the boss of a merchant band.

398
00:30:25,958 --> 00:30:28,529
I've never seen a woman boss before.

399
00:30:28,594 --> 00:30:32,041
We won't run away. Let us go.

400
00:30:32,831 --> 00:30:34,435
Shut up and follow me.

401
00:30:34,499 --> 00:30:37,207
Teach them a lesson.

402
00:30:37,269 --> 00:30:39,442
Don't worry. I will.

403
00:30:39,504 --> 00:30:41,882
Let's go. Get going.

404
00:30:41,940 --> 00:30:45,683
Hey, Young man.

405
00:30:48,447 --> 00:30:51,758
My boss wishes to talk to you.

406
00:30:51,817 --> 00:30:53,262
Do you have a minute?

407
00:30:56,555 --> 00:31:01,555
It still bothers me to have
a con artist work for me.

408
00:31:01,760 --> 00:31:05,139
We don't have a choice.

409
00:31:05,197 --> 00:31:08,076
We have to make
this deal go through.

410
00:31:13,672 --> 00:31:16,676
We'll get straight to the point.

411
00:31:17,275 --> 00:31:19,846
I heard that you speak Chinese.

412
00:31:21,680 --> 00:31:23,682
I saw you at the docks.

413
00:31:25,384 --> 00:31:27,785
There's a Chinese merchant
at our store.

414
00:31:27,786 --> 00:31:30,164
We need someone to interpret.

415
00:31:30,455 --> 00:31:33,095
Our interpreter is out of town.

416
00:31:33,291 --> 00:31:35,532
My Chinese isn't good enough.

417
00:31:38,330 --> 00:31:41,709
We need to make this deal.

418
00:31:42,801 --> 00:31:46,408
You're hiring me
for an important deal?

419
00:31:51,243 --> 00:31:52,415
Help us.

420
00:32:00,819 --> 00:32:03,163
Where is the Chinese merchant?

421
00:32:16,968 --> 00:32:19,448
We have to get
100 Chinese silver.

422
00:32:19,771 --> 00:32:22,581
How much is
that in Joseon money?

423
00:32:22,908 --> 00:32:25,445
About 400 nyang.

424
00:32:26,411 --> 00:32:30,291
A single ginseng equals
a bag of rice.

425
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:34,324
Yes, that's why it's so important.

426
00:32:37,389 --> 00:32:38,367
Let's go.

427
00:32:49,601 --> 00:32:50,807
Let's start.

428
00:32:52,604 --> 00:32:55,539
You saw the merchandise.

429
00:32:55,540 --> 00:32:57,007
Let's make a deal.

430
00:32:57,008 --> 00:32:59,110
Where are you from?

431
00:32:59,111 --> 00:33:01,312
From Shanmen

432
00:33:01,313 --> 00:33:05,916
It's not very far from here.

433
00:33:05,917 --> 00:33:09,524
Yes, about 40km.

434
00:33:11,490 --> 00:33:13,624
How much do you need?

435
00:33:13,625 --> 00:33:16,427
6 kg.

436
00:33:16,428 --> 00:33:19,773
They're from Shanmen
and they want 6 kg.

437
00:33:21,933 --> 00:33:23,879
Lower the price.

438
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:28,405
Shanmen is a close part of China,

439
00:33:28,406 --> 00:33:31,182
and there's a big black market.

440
00:33:31,576 --> 00:33:34,216
If they came all the way here,

441
00:33:34,279 --> 00:33:36,885
they're trying to get a better deal.

442
00:33:37,048 --> 00:33:41,053
We can't get 100 nyang,
ask for 90 nyang.

443
00:33:44,523 --> 00:33:47,129
How much is it for 600g?

444
00:33:49,895 --> 00:33:52,136
120 nyang.

445
00:33:56,902 --> 00:33:59,610
He asked for 120.

446
00:34:05,777 --> 00:34:07,778
80 should be enough.

447
00:34:07,779 --> 00:34:10,089
120 is too expensive.

448
00:34:11,249 --> 00:34:14,685
This is the best ginseng
in Joseon.

449
00:34:14,686 --> 00:34:16,996
I want 120.

450
00:34:18,990 --> 00:34:19,590
Hey.

451
00:34:19,591 --> 00:34:21,002
Let him go on.

452
00:34:30,902 --> 00:34:34,138
We buy Joseon ginseng all the time,

453
00:34:34,139 --> 00:34:36,473
but we never paid over 90.

454
00:34:36,474 --> 00:34:38,385
Let's settle on 90.

455
00:34:42,147 --> 00:34:46,186
110!

456
00:34:48,019 --> 00:34:50,499
That's our final offer.

457
00:35:00,498 --> 00:35:04,134
It's too expensive.
They'll walk away.

458
00:35:04,135 --> 00:35:05,409
Let's watch.

459
00:35:10,308 --> 00:35:13,010
We took a risk coming here.

460
00:35:13,011 --> 00:35:15,651
Let's settle on 95.

461
00:35:17,015 --> 00:35:20,050
If you can't accept our price,

462
00:35:20,051 --> 00:35:23,954
you can get some
from the black market.

463
00:35:23,955 --> 00:35:26,891
Ginseng sold at
the black market is illegal,

464
00:35:26,892 --> 00:35:29,532
but it is permitted in Shanmen.

465
00:35:42,774 --> 00:35:48,452
OK, we'll take 6kg at 110.

466
00:35:51,650 --> 00:35:55,223
They'll take 6kg at 110.

467
00:36:04,229 --> 00:36:05,105
This way.

468
00:36:05,931 --> 00:36:07,298
Get the 6kg ready.

469
00:36:07,299 --> 00:36:08,334
Yes, sir.

470
00:36:11,169 --> 00:36:12,512
Well done.

471
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:16,182
I was so nervous.

472
00:36:16,841 --> 00:36:18,946
The negotiations were too rash.

473
00:36:19,010 --> 00:36:21,251
There are principles
and manners in business.

474
00:36:21,313 --> 00:36:23,714
Do you think I was too rash?

475
00:36:23,715 --> 00:36:26,594
Of course. You were lucky.

476
00:36:26,651 --> 00:36:29,188
90 was enough and
you asked for 120.

477
00:36:29,254 --> 00:36:33,293
If she had not stopped me,
I would have stopped you.

478
00:36:36,328 --> 00:36:40,003
Why did you call
such a high price?

479
00:36:41,099 --> 00:36:45,673
They lied about coming
from Shanmen.

480
00:36:48,039 --> 00:36:49,575
How do you know?

481
00:36:50,241 --> 00:36:52,881
I've read that Chinese merchants

482
00:36:52,944 --> 00:36:56,824
are divided by North and South
and they're rivals.

483
00:36:57,349 --> 00:37:00,660
The Southern merchants
wear jade on their clothes

484
00:37:00,719 --> 00:37:04,132
to mark themselves from
Northern merchants.

485
00:37:04,189 --> 00:37:07,257
They had jade on their clothes.

486
00:37:07,258 --> 00:37:09,397
And they were wearing boots.

487
00:37:09,461 --> 00:37:13,102
It's the rainy season
in South China.

488
00:37:13,231 --> 00:37:15,404
The river is probably flooded

489
00:37:15,467 --> 00:37:18,141
and they have to wear boots.

490
00:37:18,770 --> 00:37:20,471
I've never seen a Shanmen merchant

491
00:37:20,472 --> 00:37:23,316
wearing such boots.

492
00:37:23,908 --> 00:37:26,354
That doesn't matter.

493
00:37:26,911 --> 00:37:28,117
It does.

494
00:37:29,514 --> 00:37:32,427
They lied about being from Shanmen

495
00:37:32,484 --> 00:37:35,488
to hide that they were in a hurry.

496
00:37:35,854 --> 00:37:40,224
When the river's flooded, Southern
merchants can't travel by land.

497
00:37:40,225 --> 00:37:42,569
They had to take a boat.

498
00:37:43,261 --> 00:37:47,107
Why do you think they went
through so much trouble?

499
00:37:47,165 --> 00:37:50,408
They weren't going back empty handed
no matter how expensive it was.

500
00:37:50,468 --> 00:37:54,245
The deal would've gone
through at 120.

501
00:37:54,305 --> 00:37:59,653
I settled on 110
for future business.

502
00:38:02,847 --> 00:38:03,917
You...

503
00:38:11,589 --> 00:38:16,026
I'd like you to interpret for us

504
00:38:16,027 --> 00:38:18,098
in all our future business
with China.

505
00:38:20,398 --> 00:38:24,234
You'll be given
an important position

506
00:38:24,235 --> 00:38:26,408
and we'll compensate you plenty.

507
00:38:27,872 --> 00:38:30,040
I have no plans
on being a merchant.

508
00:38:30,041 --> 00:38:33,454
I studied Chinese
to be an interpreter.

509
00:38:33,778 --> 00:38:35,280
Good bye.

510
00:38:47,759 --> 00:38:49,932
Hey, wait.

511
00:38:53,298 --> 00:38:55,869
This is your compensation
for the deal.

512
00:38:56,835 --> 00:38:59,403
I wasn't expecting payment.
No, thank you.

513
00:38:59,404 --> 00:39:01,850
You're so stubborn.

514
00:39:02,373 --> 00:39:06,583
Then think of it as compensation
for your friends that got beat up.

515
00:39:15,954 --> 00:39:17,194
Oh dear.

516
00:39:23,928 --> 00:39:25,464
Please forgive me.

517
00:39:30,335 --> 00:39:34,477
I missed. I won't miss again.

518
00:39:35,640 --> 00:39:37,210
Please forgive me.

519
00:39:37,775 --> 00:39:40,517
Cho-rye, what is he saying?

520
00:39:41,479 --> 00:39:42,958
I have no idea.

521
00:39:43,648 --> 00:39:45,628
I know you like him,

522
00:39:45,683 --> 00:39:48,721
but he'll make us starve to death.

523
00:39:48,786 --> 00:39:50,265
Don't hate me for this.

524
00:39:51,623 --> 00:39:55,093
I hate gamblers.

525
00:39:55,160 --> 00:39:57,367
Give him a clean death
for old time's sake.

526
00:39:58,563 --> 00:40:03,706
Cho-rye... please...

527
00:40:04,002 --> 00:40:05,135
Mang-tae.

528
00:40:05,136 --> 00:40:06,080
Yes.

529
00:40:06,471 --> 00:40:08,747
After he's dead,

530
00:40:08,806 --> 00:40:10,843
take him over the mountains

531
00:40:10,942 --> 00:40:13,218
and feed him to the crows.

532
00:40:13,278 --> 00:40:14,518
Yes.

533
00:40:14,579 --> 00:40:15,990
No, please...

534
00:40:18,716 --> 00:40:19,249
Hey.

535
00:40:19,250 --> 00:40:19,990
Yeah?

536
00:40:22,153 --> 00:40:24,599
Bok-tae... Oh...

537
00:40:32,463 --> 00:40:35,000
Jeez...

538
00:40:36,034 --> 00:40:37,172
What is it?

539
00:40:39,437 --> 00:40:40,507
I got money for their beating.

540
00:40:40,605 --> 00:40:42,846
Cut them some slack.

541
00:40:44,008 --> 00:40:44,816
Hey...

542
00:41:03,695 --> 00:41:05,971
You're home
!Yeah.

543
00:41:06,030 --> 00:41:08,010
Father's waiting for you.

544
00:41:08,533 --> 00:41:10,171
You're home late
!Yes.

545
00:41:10,235 --> 00:41:14,149
Go inside.
Your father's been waiting for you.

546
00:41:14,205 --> 00:41:16,651
He has
an important announcement.

547
00:41:47,105 --> 00:41:51,554
I'm going to be
a merchant from now.

548
00:41:56,714 --> 00:41:58,523
What do you mean?

549
00:41:58,583 --> 00:42:02,759
You've studied so hard for your goal.
You can't give up now.

550
00:42:02,854 --> 00:42:05,061
I've tried enough.

551
00:42:05,623 --> 00:42:08,035
Don't worry about making a living.

552
00:42:08,159 --> 00:42:11,572
I can still carry salt.

553
00:42:11,963 --> 00:42:16,378
No, I may have bad luck
or no talent,

554
00:42:16,868 --> 00:42:20,315
but I'm not destined
to be an interpreter.

555
00:42:22,740 --> 00:42:28,782
The envoy march to Yanjing
passes through here in a few days.

556
00:42:29,013 --> 00:42:31,584
I'll join the march as a merchant.

557
00:42:31,649 --> 00:42:37,292
You follow me to Yanjing
and see and experience China.

558
00:42:38,022 --> 00:42:40,002
If you see and experience it,

559
00:42:40,058 --> 00:42:43,160
I'll help you on your examination.

560
00:42:43,161 --> 00:42:46,631
It's illegal to leave the country.

561
00:42:46,698 --> 00:42:49,066
What if something goes wrong?

562
00:42:49,067 --> 00:42:52,336
It's OK if you're
handling the horses

563
00:42:52,337 --> 00:42:54,317
that joins the march.

564
00:42:54,839 --> 00:42:58,408
I hear you make good money

565
00:42:58,409 --> 00:43:00,787
if you sell merchandise.

566
00:43:01,412 --> 00:43:05,588
It'll be enough to pay for our trip

567
00:43:06,250 --> 00:43:10,357
and have some money left.

568
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:17,369
Father, considering our money situation,
it'll be difficult to go to Yanjing.

569
00:43:18,062 --> 00:43:20,599
You make profit
by selling merchandise,

570
00:43:20,665 --> 00:43:23,669
but we need money to buy them first.

571
00:43:24,168 --> 00:43:27,337
We'll need a lot of money.

572
00:43:27,338 --> 00:43:29,340
Where are we going to get it?

573
00:43:29,941 --> 00:43:32,478
I already have a plan.

574
00:43:50,561 --> 00:43:52,598
Do you know who lives here?

575
00:43:53,131 --> 00:43:54,235
No, Father.

576
00:43:55,700 --> 00:43:58,874
Hong Deuk-joo,
the richest man in town.

577
00:44:06,544 --> 00:44:07,522
Yes, sir.

578
00:44:11,549 --> 00:44:12,892
Can I help you?

579
00:44:13,317 --> 00:44:15,422
I'm here to see
the owner of this house.

580
00:44:17,555 --> 00:44:18,795
Follow me.

581
00:44:34,806 --> 00:44:36,149
Wait here.

582
00:44:36,707 --> 00:44:41,884
You make your guests wait
in the servant's quarters?

583
00:44:42,313 --> 00:44:44,850
You're not the only one

584
00:44:44,982 --> 00:44:46,791
who wants to see my master.

585
00:44:46,984 --> 00:44:49,692
Everyone here is waiting.

586
00:44:49,754 --> 00:44:51,131
Wait your turn.

587
00:44:56,360 --> 00:44:58,465
You have to have patience.

588
00:44:59,096 --> 00:45:01,337
I've been waiting for three days.

589
00:45:38,236 --> 00:45:40,773
Forgive me this once.

590
00:45:40,838 --> 00:45:44,411
I won't ever make another mistake.

591
00:45:44,909 --> 00:45:46,286
How's Yeon-sim?

592
00:45:46,344 --> 00:45:50,383
Huh? Who?

593
00:45:50,715 --> 00:45:53,787
That courtesan from Pyeongyang,
the one you married.

594
00:45:53,851 --> 00:45:57,731
Well...

595
00:45:58,990 --> 00:46:00,697
Actually...

596
00:46:01,125 --> 00:46:03,264
How much loss did we suffer?

597
00:46:04,328 --> 00:46:09,300
We lost 300 bags of rice

598
00:46:09,400 --> 00:46:11,573
because the ship sank.

599
00:46:12,236 --> 00:46:16,082
And 200 boxes of fish were
left rotting on the port

600
00:46:16,140 --> 00:46:18,552
because he placed the wrong order.

601
00:46:18,709 --> 00:46:20,313
How much is that?

602
00:46:20,912 --> 00:46:23,449
2,300 nyang in total.

603
00:46:23,748 --> 00:46:26,354
2,300 nyang...

604
00:46:26,417 --> 00:46:31,093
He lost that
much because of the girl.

605
00:46:31,155 --> 00:46:32,828
No, sir.

606
00:46:32,890 --> 00:46:35,734
The people who work for me...

607
00:46:35,793 --> 00:46:39,502
You idiot!

608
00:46:41,632 --> 00:46:42,770
Ouch.

609
00:46:42,867 --> 00:46:45,347
Take away all his stores,

610
00:46:45,403 --> 00:46:47,537
and confiscate the trading license.

611
00:46:47,538 --> 00:46:48,846
Yes, sir.

612
00:46:49,106 --> 00:46:50,312
Soon-tak.

613
00:46:50,708 --> 00:46:52,085
Yes, sir.

614
00:46:52,143 --> 00:46:54,089
Use him as your employee.

615
00:46:54,145 --> 00:46:56,455
Teach him from the bottom.

616
00:46:56,514 --> 00:46:57,280
Yes, sir.

617
00:46:57,281 --> 00:47:01,525
Sir, please.
Please forgive me.

618
00:47:01,586 --> 00:47:05,033
I don't want to see him.
Get him out of here.

619
00:47:05,089 --> 00:47:06,159
Yes.

620
00:47:06,223 --> 00:47:12,435
Sir, please...
Please forgive me.

621
00:47:19,637 --> 00:47:23,050
When's that envoy march
to Yanjing arriving here?

622
00:47:23,107 --> 00:47:26,645
In about 3 days.

623
00:47:27,411 --> 00:47:29,482
We should be sending someone, too.

624
00:47:30,047 --> 00:47:31,355
Of course.

625
00:47:31,849 --> 00:47:33,351
Who should I send...

626
00:47:42,693 --> 00:47:43,899
Sam-bo.

627
00:47:44,395 --> 00:47:46,341
Yes.

628
00:47:47,098 --> 00:47:48,270
You go.

629
00:47:49,300 --> 00:47:51,940
Huh? Of course.

630
00:48:04,281 --> 00:48:06,887
Next three, come with me.

631
00:48:07,084 --> 00:48:09,496
Huh?
!Yes.

632
00:48:12,990 --> 00:48:15,664
You won't be able to see him today.

633
00:48:18,663 --> 00:48:22,805
I've learned plenty about China

634
00:48:22,867 --> 00:48:26,371
from the merchants I meet.

635
00:48:26,570 --> 00:48:30,279
I know Yanjing pretty well.

636
00:48:30,941 --> 00:48:35,981
I'll pass the exam and become
the best interpreter in Joseon.

637
00:48:36,647 --> 00:48:39,753
Please don't become a merchant.

638
00:48:42,620 --> 00:48:47,228
This is enough humiliation.

639
00:48:56,033 --> 00:49:01,346
If I give you
a bowl of rice and barley,

640
00:49:01,405 --> 00:49:03,908
how would you last a month on it?

641
00:49:04,175 --> 00:49:06,621
Start with you on the right.

642
00:49:07,078 --> 00:49:10,116
I have a family of six.

643
00:49:10,181 --> 00:49:12,982
Two bowls isn't enough.

644
00:49:12,983 --> 00:49:15,293
I'll make a living by
making porridge out of it.

645
00:49:16,554 --> 00:49:18,659
What about you in the middle?

646
00:49:19,790 --> 00:49:23,567
I'll divide the rice
equally in 30 bags

647
00:49:23,627 --> 00:49:25,800
and eat one bag at a time.

648
00:49:25,863 --> 00:49:29,174
It won't be plenty, but I'll last.

649
00:49:30,367 --> 00:49:31,505
What about you?

650
00:49:31,769 --> 00:49:34,909
I'll eat all the rice I want.

651
00:49:35,506 --> 00:49:37,782
And starve for
the rest of the month?

652
00:49:37,942 --> 00:49:42,721
No, I'll have the strength to go out
and find a job to earn money.

653
00:49:45,316 --> 00:49:47,887
You two, you can leave.

654
00:49:47,952 --> 00:49:48,930
Huh?

655
00:49:49,220 --> 00:49:50,528
Get out.

656
00:49:51,322 --> 00:49:52,130
Why?

657
00:49:53,090 --> 00:49:56,003
Give 50 nyang to the big guy.

658
00:49:56,427 --> 00:49:57,667
Yes, sir.

659
00:50:02,399 --> 00:50:03,844
Next three.

660
00:50:04,235 --> 00:50:05,213
Yes.

661
00:50:09,406 --> 00:50:10,544
Get up.

662
00:50:17,648 --> 00:50:22,018
If I give you 1 nyang per person,

663
00:50:22,019 --> 00:50:24,659
how would you make
a profit in 5 days?

664
00:50:25,456 --> 00:50:26,662
You only have 5 days.

665
00:50:26,724 --> 00:50:30,228
Deuk-joo, are you in there?

666
00:50:30,628 --> 00:50:33,930
Deuk-joo, answer me.

667
00:50:33,931 --> 00:50:35,877
Where do you think are?

668
00:50:35,933 --> 00:50:37,207
Let me go.

669
00:50:37,268 --> 00:50:38,406
What's going on?

670
00:50:41,205 --> 00:50:42,912
He won't listen to me.

671
00:50:43,240 --> 00:50:45,481
Get rid of him.

672
00:50:45,643 --> 00:50:47,281
Let's go!

673
00:50:47,611 --> 00:50:48,646
Let go of him.

674
00:50:49,213 --> 00:50:50,954
Father, stop it.

675
00:50:51,015 --> 00:50:52,392
Back off!

676
00:50:53,784 --> 00:50:58,755
Deuk-joo. It's me.
Bong-haek.

677
00:50:58,756 --> 00:51:01,430
It's Lim Bong-haek
from Jincheon Village.

678
00:51:01,492 --> 00:51:03,369
Get him out of here.

679
00:51:04,028 --> 00:51:04,870
Yes.

680
00:51:05,496 --> 00:51:06,629
Take your hands off.

681
00:51:06,630 --> 00:51:08,109
Let him go.

682
00:51:18,209 --> 00:51:19,347
It's me.

683
00:51:21,445 --> 00:51:22,389
You?

684
00:51:22,980 --> 00:51:24,391
Bong-haek.

685
00:51:29,587 --> 00:51:32,864
Long time no see.
What brings you here?

686
00:51:32,923 --> 00:51:35,164
I need to borrow some money.

687
00:51:38,128 --> 00:51:40,472
Give me 500 nyang.

688
00:52:14,632 --> 00:52:16,236
Give him 500 nyang.

689
00:52:19,603 --> 00:52:22,049
What about loan documents
or collateral?

690
00:52:22,139 --> 00:52:23,550
No need.

691
00:52:29,647 --> 00:52:31,388
What are you waiting for?

692
00:52:31,715 --> 00:52:32,887
Yes.

693
00:52:37,187 --> 00:52:38,393
Is he your son?

694
00:52:38,722 --> 00:52:39,860
Yes.

695
00:52:40,658 --> 00:52:43,468
I bet he's studying to be
an interpreter too.

696
00:52:50,668 --> 00:52:52,147
It's ready.

697
00:52:52,369 --> 00:52:53,575
Give it to him.

698
00:52:53,871 --> 00:52:54,815
Yes.

699
00:52:56,140 --> 00:52:57,676
It's a check for 500 nyang.

700
00:52:57,741 --> 00:53:00,221
You can give it to any of his stores

701
00:53:00,277 --> 00:53:02,689
and they'll pay you the cash.

702
00:53:06,517 --> 00:53:09,225
I'll pay you back in 6 months.

703
00:53:12,189 --> 00:53:13,793
Let's go
!Yes.

704
00:53:29,773 --> 00:53:31,912
How do you know him?

705
00:53:33,410 --> 00:53:34,115
Father.

706
00:53:34,211 --> 00:53:35,952
It's none of your concern.

707
00:53:41,585 --> 00:53:42,495
It's good.

708
00:53:44,488 --> 00:53:46,764
I've never seen
you waste a dime

709
00:53:47,157 --> 00:53:51,230
in all the years
I've worked for you.

710
00:53:52,029 --> 00:53:53,940
Who is he?

711
00:53:53,998 --> 00:53:56,308
Why did you give him
so much money?

712
00:53:56,500 --> 00:53:59,743
I would've given 1,000 nyang
if he asked.

713
00:54:01,672 --> 00:54:06,246
I knew this day
would come someday.

714
00:54:13,517 --> 00:54:15,360
Oh, it feels good.

715
00:54:22,359 --> 00:54:26,095
Japanese silver coins?

716
00:54:26,096 --> 00:54:28,931
Yes, I'll buy Japanese silver coins

717
00:54:28,932 --> 00:54:31,934
and exchange it
with Chinese silver coins.

718
00:54:31,935 --> 00:54:34,904
It's worth more over there.

719
00:54:34,905 --> 00:54:38,182
We can make a good profit.

720
00:54:38,609 --> 00:54:41,577
When I was young,

721
00:54:41,578 --> 00:54:44,457
I saw someone make
a lot of money this way.

722
00:54:47,451 --> 00:54:49,829
I'll go buy them tomorrow
in Pyeongyang.

723
00:54:51,021 --> 00:54:53,399
It won't do any good.

724
00:54:53,957 --> 00:54:56,801
What do you mean?

725
00:54:57,361 --> 00:55:01,639
It's been decades since
Japanese silver coins were used.

726
00:55:02,399 --> 00:55:03,844
Are you sure?

727
00:55:04,435 --> 00:55:08,406
Yes, I heard it from the merchants.

728
00:55:11,842 --> 00:55:16,018
Then we have a problem.

729
00:55:19,750 --> 00:55:22,253
I've been away for so long.

730
00:55:22,820 --> 00:55:25,198
I don't know anything anymore.

731
00:55:28,559 --> 00:55:33,099
I think we should take ginseng.

732
00:55:34,131 --> 00:55:35,371
Ginseng?

733
00:55:35,699 --> 00:55:39,476
I saw merchants from South China

734
00:55:39,536 --> 00:55:41,072
who came a long way to buy ginseng.

735
00:55:41,438 --> 00:55:43,884
They came such a long way.

736
00:55:43,941 --> 00:55:47,286
That means
it's expensive over there.

737
00:55:47,678 --> 00:55:49,589
Where can we buy ginseng?

738
00:55:50,481 --> 00:55:53,516
I know a merchant in town.

739
00:55:53,517 --> 00:55:55,258
I'll try to get it.

740
00:55:58,789 --> 00:56:01,929
Sang-ok, are you home?

741
00:56:07,664 --> 00:56:09,735
What are you doing here?

742
00:56:09,833 --> 00:56:11,676
I need to talk to you.

743
00:56:15,906 --> 00:56:17,283
Come in.

744
00:56:19,376 --> 00:56:21,982
Ma'am, he asked to see you.

745
00:56:23,313 --> 00:56:24,690
Please have a seat.

746
00:56:25,482 --> 00:56:26,426
Take a seat.

747
00:56:26,683 --> 00:56:27,684
Thank you.

748
00:56:28,051 --> 00:56:29,928
Bring some tea
!Yes.

749
00:56:33,790 --> 00:56:36,168
What is it?

750
00:56:38,495 --> 00:56:40,566
I'd like to buy some ginseng.

751
00:56:50,107 --> 00:56:53,281
What for?

752
00:56:53,644 --> 00:56:55,885
We're joining the envoy
march to Yanjing

753
00:56:55,946 --> 00:56:58,722
as horse handlers.

754
00:56:58,782 --> 00:57:00,853
We'll take ginseng and sell it.

755
00:57:00,918 --> 00:57:03,296
You must be out of your mind.

756
00:57:03,987 --> 00:57:06,467
It'll be confiscated

757
00:57:06,523 --> 00:57:08,594
at the checkpoint.

758
00:57:09,159 --> 00:57:10,866
What do you mean?

759
00:57:11,628 --> 00:57:13,369
You really don't know?

760
00:57:16,867 --> 00:57:19,473
Only Hanyang merchants
and interpreters

761
00:57:19,570 --> 00:57:22,608
are allowed to bring ginseng.

762
00:57:22,739 --> 00:57:26,881
Merchants from other regions,
including ourselves, are forbidden

763
00:57:26,944 --> 00:57:30,153
to carry ginseng across borders.

764
00:57:30,547 --> 00:57:33,494
It's restricted by the law.

765
00:57:34,051 --> 00:57:37,999
That's why we sell it on the black
market because it's banned.

766
00:57:38,055 --> 00:57:40,262
The government turns
a blind eye to that.

767
00:57:41,391 --> 00:57:45,134
If I can't bring ginseng,

768
00:57:45,195 --> 00:57:47,004
what can I sell to make a profit?

769
00:57:47,564 --> 00:57:49,976
If you had your own merchant band,

770
00:57:50,033 --> 00:57:55,278
paper or wood is the best choice.

771
00:57:55,772 --> 00:57:59,743
But since you're a horse handler,
large items are out of question.

772
00:58:00,877 --> 00:58:03,221
I think tiger fur
is the best choice.

773
00:58:03,680 --> 00:58:05,125
That's right.

774
00:58:05,215 --> 00:58:07,149
It was banned once

775
00:58:07,150 --> 00:58:09,152
but they don't enforce it
these days.

776
00:58:09,820 --> 00:58:12,892
Can I get any tiger fur?

777
00:58:12,956 --> 00:58:14,594
We don't have any.

778
00:58:15,092 --> 00:58:16,559
Other merchants
probably don't either.

779
00:58:16,560 --> 00:58:18,733
It's all sold out by now.

780
00:58:24,568 --> 00:58:26,411
Thank you for your advice.

781
00:58:31,808 --> 00:58:35,187
Why don't you do
business with me?